{
  "_doc": "The MediaPipe Hands geometry, recorded from the OpenCV zoo demo (opencv_zoo samples/cpp/mediapipe: MPPalmDet and MPHandPose, Apache-2.0) run VERBATIM on hand_plain.png, at full float precision. NOT from this repository's own pipeline: tools/verify/verify_hands.py sections 1 and 2 both run the same front end on two backends, so between them they can only show that the container and onnxruntime agree. This file is what says the front end is the right one. There is deliberately no flag on the gate that regenerates it: a golden a file can rewrite records whatever the file currently believes, which is the one thing it must not do. LOCATION: this file is TRACKED, unlike the container and the two ONNX checkpoints beside it -- models/** is gitignored except for CHECKPOINT.json, so a golden in models/ would exist on the machine that recorded it and on no other. reference/goldens/ is where this tree keeps tracked goldens.",
